# vibedsp — THE ONE SOURCE LIST. Every build reads this file; none of them keeps its own copy.
#
# ★★★ WHY THIS EXISTS. There are FOUR builds of vibedsp and each used to list its sources by hand:
#
#     android/app/src/main/cpp/CMakeLists.txt        the Android app
#     android/app/src/main/cpp/vibedsp/test/...      the host test harness
#     vibeserver/CMakeLists.txt                      the Linux server
#     modules/vibe-local-sdr/build_ios.sh            the prebuilt iOS .a
#
# On 2026-08-02 two new files (channelizer.cpp, zoomspec.cpp) were added and reached ONE of them.
# The Linux server failed to link, then the iOS CLOUD build failed to link ten minutes and a push
# after the mistake, and the Android app would have failed next. Four hand-maintained lists agree
# only by luck, and the failure is always the same shape: the code compiles, and the linker
# complains about symbols that were never built.
#
# ★ Add a .cpp here and every build picks it up. That is the whole point — do not re-list it
#   anywhere else.
# ★ HOW IT IS PARSED: every reader takes ONLY lines that look like a filename — no spaces, ending
#   in .cpp. So blank lines and comments are ignored WHATEVER they contain, and you may write
#   freely here. That rule replaced "skip lines starting with #", which broke the moment a comment
#   contained a SEMICOLON: CMake lists are semicolon-separated, so the line split in two and the
#   tail was read as a source file (2026-08-02, found immediately by the tests failing to link).
#   One filename per line, relative to this directory.
# ★ NOT listed here: third_party/kissfft/*.c. Each build compiles those its own way — iOS and
#   Android rename the symbols to vibe_* so they cannot clash with ft8_lib's own copy of KissFFT.

fft.cpp
channelizer.cpp
zoomspec.cpp
ddc.cpp
resampler.cpp
stereo.cpp
rds.cpp
pipeline.cpp
